{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Will I send against you.</b> Incite against you, and likewise ״וְשֵׁן בְּהֵמוֹת אֲשַׁלַּח בָּם״ (Deuteronomy 32) — a term of inciting; אינציט\"ר בְּלַעַ\"ז." "<b>The mixture.</b> All kinds of wild beasts, snakes, and scorpions, mixed together — and they would ravage them. And there is a reason behind this in the aggadah, for each and every plague — why this one and why that one: in the strategies of the wars of kings He came upon them, in the order of a kingdom when it besieges a city. First he ruins its water supply, and afterward they sound the alarm against them and blow the shofars to frighten them and to dismay them — and likewise the frogs croak and clamor, etc., as is found in Midrash Rabbi Tanchuma (parashat Bo)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {0 "the la'az is Old French enciter, 'to incite'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:51:07.118949985Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}